# file now vets as its `expected` line says it should. Kept as the
# regression guard; the shared rows are vet-sizing-* and
# vet-must-over-a-container-* in test/spec/vet.tsv.
#
# C5 (use-case 09): list form -- length(max(2)) & unique() beside a list
# spread template are stripped when the schema settles (--canon of this
# file alone: {"labels":[&:string]}), so duplicate and oversize data
# vets valid. One-document evaluation of the same atoms with the same
# list refuses ([aontu/constraint], exit 1). Bare unique()/length(max)
# WITHOUT the template in the same conjunct are correctly re-checked.
# expected: verdict: invalid, exit 1 (3 elements > max(2), and "a","a"
#           violates unique())
# actual: verdict: valid, exit 0
# run: aontu vet list-sizing-dropped.aon dup-labels.json
labels: [&: string] & length(max(2)) & unique()
